## Issues Resolved vs. Remaining

### Resolved
- No more SPOF at the load balancer tier.
- No more resource contention between web, app, and database layers.
- Each component can be scaled, patched, and restarted independently.

### Still Present / Next Steps
- The database server remains a single node. A Primary-Replica pair with automatic failover (e.g., MySQL MHA or Orchestrator) should be added.
- SSL termination still happens at the load balancer; end-to-end encryption to the web server tier is not yet configured.
- Firewalls and monitoring agents should be applied to each of the new dedicated servers as described in task 2.
